Pit scouting interviews are what teams say about themselves: use them for archetype and preferred role, but trust match notes and EPA over them.

Scouting notes are a small, uneven sample; EPA is measured over every match a team has played. Where a team has few or no notes, lean on its EPA and say the read is thin instead of guessing. Do not write a team off, or call it a threat, on the strength of one or two notes.

